personal/probe — attribution
============================

lib/classifier.ts
-----------------
The trajectory lexicon, its scoring weights, and the `minimal-like` /
`standard-like` / `ambiguous` thresholds are ported from:

  yjh051108/dsh-router-standard — probe/classifier.mjs
  https://github.com/yjh051108/dsh-router-standard
  MIT License

which states that it mirrors:

  xiaobright/modeltest — evaluator/trigger_probe/src/classifier.mjs
  https://github.com/xiaobright/modeltest
  MIT License

The weights are kept byte-for-byte on purpose: identical weights are what
make a number produced here comparable with the numbers those projects
published. The added aggregates (`weOnlyShare`, `letMeShare`, `languageOf`)
and the documented recalibration caveat are this fork's.

replay-first-request.ts
-----------------------
The idea of a first-request condition matrix comes from the same repository's
probe/matrix.mjs (MIT). The implementation here is not a port: upstream sends
hand-written tool-schema fixtures, while this script lifts the exact system
prompt and tool schemas from a stored session's `request/header` events and
controls the output cap as a separate flag.

Everything else
---------------
lib/log.ts, lib/phases.ts, lib/endpoint.ts, analyze-session.ts, and
compare-presets.ts are original to this fork. The phase contract encodes the
behavior of apps/cli/config/agent-presets/anchored-standard/, and the session
container is read through the harness's own frame scanner in
packages/session/session-persistence-jsonl/.
